   "evidence": "The proof only uses that algebraMap is injective and that v can be cancelled; neither Clifford structure nor invertibility of v is needed. The only callers are MonomialGroup.lean:341 and :355, and both have `hunit i : IsUnit _`, which gives the `\u2260 0` hypothesis.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/CliffordAlgebra/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Restate as `theorem even_of_neg_one_pow_smul_eq_self [Ring R] [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Invertible (2 : R)] {v : N} (hv : v \u2260 0) (h : (-1 : R) ^ n \u2022 v = v) : Even n` in a general module file. At the call sites (MonomialGroup.lean:341, 355) pass `(hunit i).ne_zero`, and drop the local `hneg` derivation in `basis_comm_monomial_iff`.",
   "issue": "`even_of_neg_one_pow_smul_eq_self` requires `IsUnit v`, `hneg : (-1 : R) \u2260 1`, and a Clifford algebra, but the statement holds for any `v \u2260 0` in any `R`-module with `[Invertible (2 : R)]`: for odd n, `-v = v` gives `2 \u2022 v = 0`, so `v = \u215f2 \u2022 2 \u2022 v = 0`.",
   "line": 50
  }
